---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '@components/container.astro';
import Sectionhead from '@components/sectionhead.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import Ava from '@assets/images/gardening.png'; // Adjust the path as needed
---

<Layout title='Digital Garden'>
  <Container>
    <Sectionhead>
      <Fragment slot='title'>What is a Digital Garden ?</Fragment>
      <!-- <Fragment slot='desc'>An over-view of my "why" for using a digital garden, what it is  and links to other relevent tooling. </Fragment> -->
      <Fragment slot='desc'
        >Discontent is the first step in the progress of a man or a nation. -
        Oscar Wilde</Fragment
      >
    </Sectionhead>

    <div class='max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16'>
      <div class='md:flex md:items-center gap-16 mb-10'>
        <div class='text-pretty leading-9'>
          <h2 class='text-4xl font-bold mb-4'>Progress is a process.</h2>
          <div class='text-lg text-slate-500'>
            <p class='mb-4'>
              I have started and stopped over the years a couple times well,
              ended up with flashcards, notes and github repos with half
              finished or unexplained ideas. This kinda left a bitter taste in
              my mouth, as I was not able to track my progress/growth and it
              comes off as somewhat unprofessional. Let's not even talk about
              the imposter syndrome that comes with it. Coming across the
              concept of a digital garden and with a background in agriculture,
              I was intrigued by the idea of a place to grow ideas, record my
              thoughts and share them with the world, a digital garden.
            </p>
            <p class='mb-4'>
              My digital garden is a place where I can plant, nuture and grow my
              thoughts, ideas, and notes. It is a place where I can grow my
              knowledge and share it with the world. It is a place where I can
              be myself and express myself freely~ish. Here is a link to its
              current iteration, <a
                href='https://garden.developingdvlpr.com/'
                class='animate-pulse text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline'
                target='_blank'
                rel='noopener'>
                my digital garden.</a
              >
            </p>
            <p class='mb-4'>
              So here are some resources that I have found useful in creating my
              digital garden:
            </p>
            <ul class='list-inside mb-4'>
              <li>
                <a
                  href='https://maggieappleton.com/garden-history'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'
                  class='text-blue animate-bounce dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline'
                  >Why it's important to have a digital garden <Icon
                    class='w-5 h-5'
                    style='display: inline;'
                    name='bx:link-external'
                  />.</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  href='https://joelhooks.com/digital-garden'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'
                  class='text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline'
                  >A good example of a digital garden <Icon
                    class='w-5 h-5'
                    style='display: inline;'
                    name='bx:link-external'
                  />.</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  href='https://nesslabs.com/digital-garden-setup'
                  target='_blank'
                  rel='noopener'
                  class='text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline'
                  >Resources for setting up a digital garden <Icon
                    class='w-5 h-5'
                    style='display: inline;'
                    name='bx:link-external'
                  />.</a
                >
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <Image
          src={Ava}
          alt='image of a garden'
          height={700}
          width={400}
          class='rounded-3xl mx-4 md:mx-0'
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
